+# Trusted local adapter
+Public __init__.py handles the explicitly accepted local console confirmation.
+Core owns permissions and every mutation. No SQL here. Display canonical escaped
+JSON, accept explicit terminal confirmation only, and bind the result to the exact
+preview. No free approval flags, file/model assertions or piped approvals.
+Trusted local-chat applications may use the Core in-process authorization seam
+after actual owner permission; no duplicate identity confirmation is required.
+This is a single-owner local application, not hostile same-user process isolation.
+END_OF_FILE: src/zaratustra/local/AGENTS.md
